def check_identical(list1, list2):
    # Check if both lists have the same length
    if len(list1) != len(list2):
        return False

    # Compare each element in the first list with the corresponding element in the second list
    for i in range(len(list1)):
        if tuple(list1[i]) != tuple(list2[i]):
            return False

    # If all elements match, the lists are identical
    return True
```
This solution checks if two lists of tuples are identical by comparing their lengths and then iterating through each element to ensure that every corresponding element is equal. If any element differs, it returns `False`, indicating that the lists are not identical. Otherwise, it returns `True`.

