def min_Num(arr, target):
    # Calculate the difference between the target and the current element
    diff = abs(target - arr[0])

    # Iterate through the array starting from the second element
    for i in range(1, len(arr)):
        if arr[i] % 2 != 0: 
            # If the current element is odd, subtract its value from the difference
            diff -= arr[i]

    # Return the absolute value of the calculated difference
    return abs(diff)
```
This solution iterates through the array, checking each element's parity (odd or even). If an element is odd, it subtracts its value from the total difference calculated so far. This ensures that the final result will always be an even number when added back to the original array.

