def check_min_heap(arr):
    # Check if all elements in the array are less than or equal to their parent
    for i in range(len(arr)):
        if arr[i] > arr[(i + 1) // 2]:
            return False
    return True
```
This solution checks each element in the array to ensure it is less than or equal to its parent. If any element violates this condition, the function returns `False`, indicating that the array does not represent a valid min heap. Otherwise, it returns `True`.

